Version: beta-v1.2.0
Changelog: |
  This release introduces transactional atomic staging and update rollbacks,
  automated configuration and cache migrations, provider sidecar tracking
  with on-the-fly provider switching, OS compatibility badges for depot selection,
  and a comprehensive offline verification test suite.

  Highlights:
  - Added atomic staging, transactional installation, and automatic rollbacks
    to the auto-updater to prevent partial installs and file corruption.
  - Added atomic file writing, backup staging, and directory merge utilities.
  - Implemented automated configuration and cache migration engines with declarative
    YAML rule processing.
  - Added provider sidecar tracking (.provider) and runtime /change-provider
    endpoint for dynamic Lua download provider switching.
  - Added operating system metadata badges (Windows, Linux, macOS) to the depot
    selection interface.
  - Enhanced depot selection script with injection deduplication and custom
    provider URL support.
  - Added robust JSON string decoding and escape sequence handling in CEF hooks.
  - Included accela-helper binary and injection scripts in production releases.
  - Hardened uninstaller (uninstall.sh) with category-based isolation,
    idempotency, and strict preservation of user manifests and luas.
  - Added comprehensive offline test suite covering migration, update verification,
    tamper detection, rollback, and uninstallation safety.

